# python -- needed by glibc's own configure, which refuses to run without it:
#   "These critical programs are missing or too old: bison python"
#
# It was a chapter-7 temporary tool in duct/chroot and never a package, which
# meant duct/builder could not rebuild glibc at all.
SRC_URL=$PYTHON_URL
SRC_SHA256=$PYTHON_SHA256
SRC_DIR=$PYTHON_SRCDIR

# --without-ensurepip because pip would reach the network during the build, and
# nothing in Duct needs it yet. --enable-shared so anything embedding Python
# links against libpython rather than statically absorbing it.
# py_cv_module__ssl=n/a disables the ssl module explicitly, and it has to be
# explicit. Python probes for OpenSSL and builds _ssl if it finds any, so
# whether this package built used to depend on whether openssl happened to be
# installed in the container at the time -- it was not, so _ssl was skipped and
# nobody noticed. The moment openssl was ordered before python, the build
# started failing:
#
#   Modules/_ssl.c:1364: error: invalid use of incomplete typedef
#                        'ASN1_OCTET_STRING'
#
# OpenSSL 4.0 made ASN1_OCTET_STRING and ASN1_IA5STRING opaque; Python 3.13's
# _ssl reaches directly into them. The two versions do not fit together, so the
# module is refused deliberately rather than left to depend on build-order
# accident. See install.sh for what that costs.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--enable-shared --without-ensurepip --without-static-libpython --enable-optimizations=no py_cv_module__ssl=n/a"
